            <div xml:id="d665">

                <pb facs="0727" n="623" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg623"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102 S/1020a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-23T18:00:00-05:00">March 23, 1932—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>114. For the Minister. Shanghai’s 196, March 23, 5 p.m., paragraph 2. The
                    Department is of opinion that neither you nor the Consul General should give any
                    encouragement to the proposal that Raven
                    resign as a protest against the outcome of the municipal elections, as such
                    action on his part might add, at a most inopportune time, another complication
                    to the present difficult situation at Shanghai. Inform Cunningham.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
